                                "sense_id": "0232e389-3504-37c7-9be1-853f8050207d",
                                "text": "As young as I am, I have obſeru'd theſe three Swaſhers: I am Boy to them all three, but all they three, though they would ſerue me, could not be Man to me; for indeed three ſuch Antiques do not amount to a man: [...]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42b46fab-3560-45f3-a234-2f0c349d9cf0",
                                "sense_id": "0232e389-3504-37c7-9be1-853f8050207d",
                                "text": "[I]f they keepe their wits, yet they are accompted fooles by reaſon of their carriage, becauſe they cannot ride a horſe, which euery Clowne can doe; ſalute and court a Gentlewoman, carue at table, cringe and make congies, which euery common ſwaſher can doe, [...]"
                            }
